{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q15211075","formula":"C₈H₁₁Cl₂N₃O₂","hill":"C8H11Cl2N3O2","elements":["H","C","N","O","Cl"],"composition":{"C":8.0,"H":11.0,"N":3.0,"O":2.0,"Cl":2.0},"names":{"en":"Uracil mustard","ru":"Урамустин"},"descriptions":{"en":"Uramustine (INN) or uracil mustard is a chemotherapy drug which belongs to the class of alkylating agents. It is used in lymphatic malignancies such as non-Hodgkin's lymphoma. It works by damaging DNA, primarily in cancer cells that preferentially take up the uracil due to their need to make nucleic acids during their rapid cycles of cell division.","ru":"Урамустин, иначе называемый хлорэтиламиноурацил, урацил мустард, допан — в настоящее время уже устаревший цитостатический противоопухолевый химиотерапевтический лекарственный препарат алкилирующего типа действия. Производное одновременно бис-β-хлорэтиламина и нуклеотида урацила."},"fame":11,"pubchemCid":6194,"mass":252.09,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1=C(C(=O)NC(=O)N1)N(CCCl)CCCl","inchikey":"IDPUKCWIGUEADI-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"5-[bis(2-chloroethyl)amino]-1H-pyrimidine-2,4-dione","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"6194","atoms":26,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":3.719,"y":-2.846,"z":0.237,"el":"Cl"},{"x":1.47,"y":3.096,"z":0.935,"el":"Cl"},{"x":-0.244,"y":0.065,"z":2.123,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.211,"y":-0.701,"z":-0.101,"el":"O"},{"x":1.159,"y":0.251,"z":-0.244,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.232,"y":-0.319,"z":1.022,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.28,"y":-0.389,"z":-1.312,"el":"N"},{"x":2.089,"y":-0.66,"z":0.412,"el":"C"},{"x":1.757,"y":1.28,"z":-1.086,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.183,"y":0.013,"z":-0.256,"el":"C"},{"x":2.573,"y":-1.732,"z":-0.551,"el":"C"},{"x":1.182,"y":2.651,"z":-0.766,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.866,"y":-0.074,"z":1.072,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.934,"y":-0.15,"z":-1.353,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.999,"y":-0.48